(4318167, 619771, 63267, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by NikonJeb:</b></div><hr/><i> I don''t know what this is, but it''s NOT a stock Shelby, if a Shelby at all. I have some terrific images of the real thing, in black, white, and ragtop if you want to see the differences. That aside, good imagery.....I like the white negative space. Really well executed. 7 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Looking at the outtakes, this sure looks like a real Shelby to me.  I would sure like to see the difference between this and a real Shelby.<br/> <br/>Sorry about the DQ Joe.  It appears the DQ''s were heavy when it comes to brightening or darkening images in this challenge and that is a shame.  But, as we all know, it happens.  I see you are putting some nice photos up with that D40 of yours.  If only this site would run DPL2 so we can put it to some good use for the team.  Sigh...oh well.<br/> <br/>Congrats on a great shot anyway.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-12-19 05:13:18.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by NikonJeb: I don''t know what this is, but it''s NOT a stock Shelby, if a Shelby at all. I have some terrific images of the real thing, in black, white, and ragtop if you want to see the differences. That aside, good imagery.....I like the white negative space. Really well executed. 7   Looking at the outtakes, this sure looks like a real Shelby to me.  I would sure like to see the difference between this and a real Shelby. Sorry about the DQ Joe.  It appears the DQ''s were heavy when it comes to brightening or darkening images in this challenge and that is a shame.  But, as we all know, it happens.  I see you are putting some nice photos up with that D40 of yours.  If only this site would run DPL2 so we can put it to some good use for the team.  Sigh...oh well. Congrats on a great shot anyway.', '2007-12-17 07:27:19.000000', '2007-12-19 05:13:18.000000', 0),
